Proposed Phases & Milestones
Phase 1: 🔐 JWT Authentication, Outgoing SMTP, and Data Isolation
Goal: Enable bulletproof JWT authentication, dynamically toggle real/mock email verification, and secure all backend endpoints with strict user-level data isolation.
Backend Changes (core_service):
Dependencies: Add djangorestframework-simplejwt to requirements.txt.
Settings: Add JWT configurations to settings.py and register simplejwt.authentication.JWTAuthentication.
SMTP Configuration: Enable dynamic toggle in settings.py loading EMAIL_BACKEND (Console/SMTP), host, port, TLS, and App Passwords from environment variables (.env).
Models:
Add UserProfile with fields: is_verified (Boolean), verification_code (6-digit OTP), reset_code (6-digit OTP).
Add UserDevice model with user, device_token, and device_type.
APIs (apps/api.py):
Register endpoints: /api/auth/register/, /api/auth/login/, /api/auth/verify-email/, /api/auth/forgot-password/, /api/auth/reset-password/.
Secure existing ViewSets under IsAuthenticated global permissions.
Modify get_queryset on all ViewSets to strictly filter data by self.request.user:
python

def get_queryset(self):
    return self.queryset.filter(user=self.request.user)
Automatically assign request.user on all record creations.
Email Utility: Create apps/utils/emails.py using EmailMultiAlternatives to compile and send premium HTML verification and reset templates.
Frontend Web Changes (client):
Configure Axios interceptor in api_core.js to automatically read the JWT token from localStorage and inject the Authorization: Bearer <token> header.
Create modern, elegant pages:
/register (Registration Page capturing dynamic or mock device tokens).
/login (Glassmorphism Login with dynamic errors & password toggles).
/verify-email (6-digit dynamic OTP input blocks).
/forgot-password & /reset-password (Sleek password reset forms).
Build a PrivateRoute routing guard redirecting unauthenticated users to /login.
Phase 2: ✍️ Interactive Database Entry Forms (All 6 Cards)
Goal: Allow users to add and manage custom entries on each of their dashboard cards, permanently storing transactions, loans, assets, lendings, and EMIs to Postgres.
Backend Changes (core_service):
Register /api/categories/ Router ViewSet and Serializer to manage transaction categories.
Frontend Web Changes (client):
Build gorgeous slide-in/fade-in modal entry forms on the following screens:
Income & Expense Pages: Dropdown selection of user categories. Checks if category exists; if not, calls /api/categories/ dynamically first, then submits transaction.
EMI Page: Dynamic dropdown of existing Loans fetched from the backend. Posts to /api/emi-payments/ with due dates and custom amounts.
Loans Page: Inputs for Principal, Interest %, Start Date, Tenure, and calculated monthly EMI.
Lendings Page: Selects Person Name, Debt Type (GIVEN / TAKEN), amount, due dates, and status.
Investments Page: Enter Asset name, Symbol, Quantity, and Average Buy Price. Automatically updates real-time quotes.
