Phase 5: 📱 React Native Mobile App (Android SMS Auto-Tracker)
Goal: Create a lightweight, battery-optimized Android app that reads transaction SMS, parses details locally, and syncs offline records to Django.
Mobile App Stack: React Native (bare CLI or optimized Expo), SQLite for local storage, react-native-get-sms-android or custom native receiver.
Core Mechanisms:
BroadcastReceiver Integration: Registers an OS-level listener that only wakes up the application when a new SMS is received. 0% background CPU idle battery usage!
Regex Parser Engine: Instantly parses banking SMS:
Pattern: Spans typical UPI, credit, and debit formats to parse: Amount, Vendor Name (e.g., Zomato, Swiggy), and Source (e.g., Bank name).
Offline Sync Handler: Writes transaction locally to SQLite. When internet status transitions to active, triggers a HeadlessJS background sync process uploading data in batches to Django /api/transactions/.
Size Optimization: Proguard active, splits architecture binaries, strips unused node_modules, yielding a highly compact APK size (<15MB).
Verification & Deployment Plan
